<main id="main">

<section class="lx-hero"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1771730728574-fbbec85da1fe?auto=format&fit=crop&w=900&h=900&q=75" alt="woman holding a black handbag, seated outdoors" width="900" height="900" fetchpriority="high"></figure><div class="lx-hero-t"><p class="lx-sm">The leather bag journal</p><h1>Know your leather. Keep it for life.</h1><p>Luxoria is an independent guide to what fine bags are made of and how to look after them. Identify a leather, treat a stain correctly and choose the right size for a weekend away.</p><p class="lx-acts"><a class="btn" href="#tools">Use the tools</a><a class="lx-text" href="leather-types-guide.html">Read about leather types</a></p></div></section>

<section class="lx-s"><div class="lx-c lx-intro"><p class="lx-quote">A good leather bag does not wear out. It wears in, provided someone takes ten minutes a season to care for it.</p><div class="lx-facts"><div><b>4</b><span>main leather finishes cover almost every bag you will meet</span></div><div><b>10 min</b><span>of care each season is enough for a bag in daily use</span></div><div><b>24 hrs</b><span>is how long a wet bag should dry before it is used again</span></div></div></div></section>

<section class="lx-s lx-blush"><div class="lx-c"><p class="lx-sm lx-mid">Four families</p><h2 class="lx-mid">The leathers you are most likely to own</h2><div class="lx-types"><article><h3>Smooth full-grain</h3><p>Natural surface with visible pores. Marks easily, ages beautifully. Needs conditioning a few times a year.</p><span>Patina: yes</span></article><article><h3>Pebbled or corrected</h3><p>Embossed with an even grain and sealed with pigment. Hides scratches and shrugs off rain.</p><span>Patina: little</span></article><article><h3>Saffiano and coated</h3><p>Cross-hatch texture pressed into a wax or resin finish. Stiff, structured and very easy to wipe clean.</p><span>Patina: none</span></article><article><h3>Suede and nubuck</h3><p>Brushed to a velvety nap. Soft and rich in colour, but dislikes water and grease. Brush, never wipe.</p><span>Patina: darkens</span></article></div></div></section>

<section class="lx-s" id="tools"><div class="lx-c"><p class="lx-sm">Three small tools</p><h2>Practical answers</h2>
<div class="lx-tool"><div class="lx-tool-n">I</div><div class="lx-tool-f"><h3>Leather Type Finder</h3><p>Two observations are usually enough to name a leather.</p><label for="lt-s">The surface looks and feels<select id="lt-s"><option value="smooth">Smooth, with tiny natural pores</option><option value="pebble">Evenly pebbled or grained</option><option value="cross">Firm, with a fine cross-hatch pattern</option><option value="nap">Soft and velvety, changes shade when stroked</option><option value="gloss">Glassy and mirror-bright</option></select></label><label for="lt-w">A drop of water on a hidden spot<select id="lt-w"><option value="soak">Darkens the leather within seconds</option><option value="bead">Sits on top as a bead</option></select></label></div><div class="lx-tool-o" id="lt-o" aria-live="polite"></div></div>
<div class="lx-tool"><div class="lx-tool-n">II</div><div class="lx-tool-f"><h3>Stain First-Aid Finder</h3><p>What to do in the first few minutes, and what to avoid.</p><label for="sa-s">The mark is<select id="sa-s"><option value="water">A water or rain mark</option><option value="oil">Grease or oil</option><option value="ink">Ballpoint ink</option><option value="makeup">Make-up or lipstick</option><option value="dye">Colour rubbed off from denim</option><option value="mould">Mould or mildew</option></select></label><label for="sa-l">The leather is<select id="sa-l"><option value="finished">Finished: pebbled, saffiano or coated</option><option value="aniline">Smooth, untreated full-grain</option><option value="suede">Suede or nubuck</option></select></label></div><div class="lx-tool-o" id="sa-o" aria-live="polite"></div></div>
<div class="lx-tool"><div class="lx-tool-n">III</div><div class="lx-tool-f"><h3>Weekender Capacity Planner</h3><p>The size of travel bag your trip really needs.</p><label for="wk-n">Nights away<input id="wk-n" type="number" min="1" max="10" value="2" inputmode="numeric"></label><label for="wk-s">Season<select id="wk-s"><option value="warm">Warm weather</option><option value="cold">Cold weather</option></select></label><label for="wk-x">Extra pairs of shoes<select id="wk-x"><option value="0">None</option><option value="1" selected>One</option><option value="2">Two</option></select></label></div><div class="lx-tool-o" id="wk-o" aria-live="polite"></div></div>
</div></section>

<section class="lx-s lx-dark"><div class="lx-c lx-pair"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1762331227611-2cfdd919b7bf?auto=format&fit=crop&w=440&h=580&q=75" alt="woman in sunglasses and a coat carrying a tote bag" width="440" height="580" loading="lazy"></figure><div><p class="lx-sm">Everyday habits</p><h2>The five-minute weekly routine</h2><ol class="lx-rout"><li>Empty the bag and shake out the lining.</li><li>Wipe the outside with a soft, dry cloth, handles first.</li><li>Check corners and the base for scuffs or damp.</li><li>Close zips and clasps so the bag keeps its shape.</li><li>Stand it upright on a shelf, not on the floor or a hook.</li></ol></div><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1732613842353-0fccc5b72d51?auto=format&fit=crop&w=440&h=580&q=75" alt="brown leather bag and a coffee cup on a table" width="440" height="580" loading="lazy"></figure></div></section>

<section class="lx-s"><div class="lx-c"><p class="lx-sm">In depth</p><h2>The guides</h2><div class="lx-gds"><a href="leather-types-guide.html"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1732613838116-6bba82321709?auto=format&fit=crop&w=640&h=420&q=75" alt="brown bag resting on a stack of books" width="640" height="420" loading="lazy"><div><span>Guide One</span><h3>The Leather Types Guide</h3><p>Grades, finishes and tanning explained, with the care each one needs.</p></div></a><a href="leather-stain-guide.html"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1711972765301-c917d4891b75?auto=format&fit=crop&w=640&h=420&q=75" alt="brown purse on a table" width="640" height="420" loading="lazy"><div><span>Guide Two</span><h3>The Stain Care Guide</h3><p>Water, oil, ink and colour transfer: what works, what makes it worse and when to stop.</p></div></a></div></div></section>

<section class="lx-s lx-blush"><div class="lx-c lx-tblw"><div><p class="lx-sm">Side by side</p><h2>Finishes compared</h2><p>No finish is best. Each exchanges some natural character for some protection, and the right one depends on how you live with your bag.</p></div><div class="tblw"><table class="lx-tbl"><thead><tr><th>Finish</th><th>Scratches</th><th>Rain</th><th>Care</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Aniline full-grain</td><td>Shows them</td><td>Marks</td><td>Regular</td></tr><tr><td>Semi-aniline</td><td>Some</td><td>Light showers</td><td>Moderate</td></tr><tr><td>Pigmented, pebbled</td><td>Hides them</td><td>Good</td><td>Low</td></tr><tr><td>Saffiano</td><td>Very resistant</td><td>Very good</td><td>Wipe only</td></tr><tr><td>Patent</td><td>Scuffs show</td><td>Excellent</td><td>Wipe only</td></tr><tr><td>Suede, nubuck</td><td>Brush out</td><td>Poor</td><td>Brush, protect</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></section>

<section class="lx-s"><div class="lx-c lx-still"><div><p class="lx-sm">On the table</p><h2>Where a bag rests matters</h2><p>More damage comes from where a bag is put down than from how it is carried. Restaurant floors are wet and gritty. Hooks stretch handles. Sunny windowsills fade one side.</p><p>Give your bag a seat, a shelf or your lap. At home, a single dedicated shelf at eye level does more for its life than any product.</p></div><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1792334787239-0423d55192c4?auto=format&fit=crop&w=620&h=620&q=75" alt="brown suede handbag on a round black table" width="620" height="620" loading="lazy"></figure></div></section>

<section class="lx-s lx-blush"><div class="lx-c lx-fq"><h2 class="lx-mid">Questions we are asked</h2><div class="lx-faq"><details open><summary>What is full-grain leather?</summary><p>Full-grain leather keeps the complete outer surface of the hide, with its natural pores and markings. It is the strongest and most breathable grade, and it develops a patina, a soft sheen and deeper colour, as it is handled.</p></details><details><summary>How do I remove a water mark from a leather bag?</summary><p>Dampen a clean cloth with plain water and wipe the whole panel evenly, edge to edge, so the mark has no hard outline. Let it dry slowly at room temperature, away from heat, then condition lightly once dry.</p></details><details><summary>Can I use baby wipes or household cleaners on leather?</summary><p>No. Most contain solvents, fragrance or detergents that strip the finish and dry the leather. Use a cleaner made for leather, or a cloth barely dampened with water, and test in a hidden spot first.</p></details><details><summary>How often should a leather bag be conditioned?</summary><p>Two to four times a year for a bag in regular use, and less for coated leathers such as saffiano or patent, which only need wiping. Over-conditioning leaves leather sticky and attracts dirt.</p></details><details><summary>What is the difference between suede and nubuck?</summary><p>Both have a soft, brushed nap. Suede is made from the underside of the hide and is softer and more delicate. Nubuck is the outer side, lightly sanded, so it is tougher but shows marks in the same way.</p></details><details><summary>What size bag do I need for a weekend away?</summary><p>For two nights, a weekender of 30 to 40 litres, roughly 50 cm long, holds clothes, a second pair of shoes and a wash bag. The capacity planner above adjusts this for longer trips and colder weather.</p></details></div></div></section>

<section class="lx-s lx-letter"><div class="lx-c"><p class="lx-sm lx-mid">Four times a year</p><h2 class="lx-mid">The Luxoria Letter</h2><p class="lx-mid">A short seasonal note on leather care, sent at the turn of each season.</p><p class="lx-mid"><a class="btn" href="mailto:hello@luxoria.com?subject=The%20Luxoria%20Letter&amp;body=Please%20subscribe%20me.">Subscribe by email</a></p></div></section>

